plete. Isco delivered a pinpoint corner from the right, finding Natan , who directed his left-footed effort into the net to give Real Betis the lead just before the interval. Tactical Shifts and Defensive Resilience The second half saw Villarreal attempting to regain control through a series of tactical substitutions. Alberto Moleiro was introduced for Tajon Buchanan in the 55th minute, while Gerard no made way for Tani Oluwaseyi shortly after. Despite controlling 62% of the possession, Villarreal struggled to break down a disciplined Real Betis side that focused on closing down spaces and hitting on the counter. As the clock ticked toward the final whistle, the game became increasingly physical, with Renato Veiga receiving a yellow card for unsportsmanlike conduct. Real Betis brought on Giovani Lo Celso and Facundo Bernal to shore up the midfield, effectively neutralizing Villarreal 's creative threats. Despite intense pressure in the closing minutes and several desperate crosses into the box, the visitors held their nerve to secure a hard-fought victory on the road."
